{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:18295000 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:18295000 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"18295000","source":"MED","pmid":"18295000","pmcid":"PMC7138055","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC7138055"]},"doi":"10.1016/s0140-6736(08)60170-1","title":"Croup.","authorString":"Bjornson CL, Johnson DW.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Bjornson CL","lastName":"Bjornson","firstName":"Candice L","initials":"CL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Faculty of Medicine, University of Calgary, Calgary, AB, Canada."}]}},{"fullName":"Johnson DW","lastName":"Johnson","firstName":"David W","initials":"DW"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"9609","volume":"371","journalIssueId":1509971,"dateOfPublication":"2008 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2008,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Lancet","title":"Lancet (London, England)","essn":"1474-547X","issn":"0140-6736","isoabbreviation":"Lancet","nlmid":"2985213R"},"printPublicationDate":"2008-01-01"},"pubYear":"2008","pageInfo":"329-339","abstractText":"Most children who present with acute onset of barky cough, stridor, and chest-wall indrawing have croup. A careful history and physical examination is the best method to confirm the diagnosis and to rule out potentially serious alternative disorders such as bacterial tracheitis and other rare causes of upper-airway obstruction. Epinephrine delivered via a nebuliser is effective for temporary relief of symptoms of airway obstruction. Corticosteroids are the mainstay of treatment, and benefit is seen in children with all levels of severity of croup, including mild cases.","affiliation":"Department of Paediatrics, Faculty of Medicine, University of Calgary, Calgary, AB, Canada.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","lang